Catfish-effect-based DRL for
Energy-Efficient Joint Switchingt

    In this chapter, we propose a catfish-based deep reinforcement learning algorithm to
optimize the energy efficiency of communication networks. The flowchart of the proposed

CDRL algorithm is shown in Fig. 8, and the content of each phase is as follows:

  1. Catfish-effect-based data preparation phase: The first stage is data preprocessing,
      aimed at preparing the training data for the subsequent deep reinforcement learning

      phase by generating communication states in advance for experience replay with different
      EE criteria.

  2. Catfish-effect-based DRL training phase: The second stage is the general training

      of the catfish deep reinforcement learning with competitive periodic interventions, de-
      signed to transfer high-reward knowledge from the catfish agent to the main agent and
      to stimulate the main agent to explore and pursue better optimization strategies.

  3. Catfish-effect-Based DRL optimization of energy efficiency phase: The third
      stage uses the trained CDRL policy to optimize communication EE.


