longer-term strategic cues. This study designs two training modes for CDRL. As shown in
Fig. 4.5, in the normal training mode, the main agent and catfish agent each have independent
experience replay memories, discount factors, and reward mechanisms, training independently

without interference. As shown in Fig. 4.6, after a random period, the system enters the


                                                                            32
intervention training mode. In this mode, a portion of the high EE experiences collected by
the catfish agent is sampled and mixed into the main agent’s training batches.The main agent

performs standard policy updates on the entire mixed batch as usual. However, since the
batch contains high EE state-action pairs, experience-driven knowledge transfer is achieved.
In the mixed batch S mix = S M ∪ S CF , 70% of the samples are drawn from the main replay

memory S M , and 30% from the catfish replay memory S CF , where S M ∈ DM , S CF ∈ DCF .
By orchestrating the above three components and the two-mode schedule, the catfish agent
persistently supplies high-value trajectories while safeguarding the main policy from premature

convergence.

A. Catfish Strategy 1: Experience Stratification

    The purpose of experience stratification is to establish an elite challenger role by posi-
tioning the catfish agent as the “ignition point for high-level experiences”, thereby attracting
other users or agents to challenge upward. This action provides different training data to

the main agent and the catfish agent, assigning distinct tasks at each experience level. This
strategy guides the main agent to adjust its policy by observing the catfish agent’s behavior.
It enables both agents to better exploit their respective discount-factor characteristics during

learning. Experiences with higher EE are stored in the catfish replay memory, while those
with moderate EE are stored in the main replay memory, allowing the catfish agent to focus on
”high-quality experiences” during training. The experience stratification flowchart is shown

in Fig. 4.7 We package the randomly generated communication scenarios into datasets and
use EE as the label to determine their storage locations. The threshold EEhigh is set as the

top 20% of the overall pre-generated data in phase 4.1, while EEmin is set as the top 50%
performance of the pre-generated data.


