Chapter 5

Experimental Result

    In this chapter, the experimental setup is explained in section 5.1 and the performance

evaluation is discussed in section 5.2, the ablation studies are presented in section 5.3, and
the RIS simulator is introduced in section 5.4.


5.1     Experimental Setup

    This section details the environment setup used for training the proposed model. The
experiments are conducted on a system running Windows 10 as the underlying operating

system. The programming environment is built using Python 3.8.16, with NumPy 1.26.4
and PyTorch 2.3.1 to support the implementation of reinforcement learning algorithms. All
training and evaluation processes are performed using an NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2080 Ti

GPU to ensure computational efficiency. The downlink communication system environment
is configured in accordance with [10], with detailed parameters listed in Table 5.1.


5.2     Performance analysis

    This section presents a performance comparison between the proposed approach and its
rivals. The experiments are divided into four scenarios based on active/passive RIS and the

presence or absence of element switching. We use the energy efficiency and sum rate defined
in chapter 3 as performance metrics. These performance metrics are:



