The catfish ablation shows a small positive contribution from the competitive reward, not a reported zero or negative result. Other papers explicitly accept tradeoffs: one load-balancing component lowers throughput under overload, and one assignment paper chooses the cheaper algorithm despite a roughly 1% loss to a broader search. I’ll keep those findings tied to their own metrics and comparators.
